 "defaultCounty": "new-york-city",
 "singular": [
  "New York registers passenger cars for two years at a time, with a fee set by weight in 100-pound steps, from $26 under 1,651 lb to $140 from 6,951 lb [fees].",
  "Twelve counties around New York City (the five boroughs, Dutchess, Nassau, Orange, Putnam, Rockland, Suffolk and Westchester) add a Metropolitan Commuter Transportation District fee of $50 per two-year registration [fees].",
  "Most counties also charge a vehicle use tax with registration: $10 per two years under 3,501 lb and $20 above in upstate counties, $30 in New York City, up to $60 in Suffolk and Westchester for heavier cars [fees].",
  "Sales tax combines the 4% state rate with the county or city rate of your address, from 7% in Saratoga, Warren and Washington counties to 8.875% in New York City [pub718].",
  "A trade-in a dealer takes for resale reduces the taxable price, but manufacturers' rebates do not [tb-trade].",
  "A first registration adds a $25 plate fee and a $50 title certificate fee [fees].",
  "Every car is inspected every 12 months and at each change of owner; the emissions test skips cars under two model years, over 25, and electric cars [inspections].",
  "The maximum inspection fee is $10 for safety plus $27 for the emissions test in the New York Metropolitan Area, or $11 elsewhere [vs77]."
 ],
